    <h2>What I collect</h2>
    <p>If you sign up, your email address, plus whether you open or click my emails. Visit counts on the site are anonymous and use no cookies.</p>
    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>To send you new videos and the occasional note from me, and to see which ones help.</p>
    <h2>Who handles it</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which also counts visits anonymously. My email list runs on Kit, which stores your address and tracks opens and clicks. Videos play from YouTube in its privacy-enhanced mode. When a video page loads, YouTube gets your IP address and can store data in your browser. Google says views in this mode aren't used to personalise your YouTube experience or ads, and it handles the data under its own privacy policy. Memberships run on Patreon and purchases on Lemon Squeezy, so if you join or buy, they handle your payment details, not me.</p>
